// Delegation suite — does the model use the `agent` tool the way its
// description asks? NOT part of the gate. Run it after touching the agent
// tool's description, against a weak and a strong model:
//
//   pnpm eval delegation --trials 3 --model minimax/MiniMax-M3
//   pnpm eval delegation --trials 3 --model anthropic/claude-opus-5
//
// Every case is sandboxed (a `files` fixture), because `agent` is not a
// read-only tool: explore mode hides it, so an unsandboxed case could never
// see it. Three questions:
//   - over-delegation: a single read or search must not spawn a sub-agent
//   - foreground vs background: an answer needed now stays foreground;
//     "don't wait" goes to run_in_background; parallel work is two calls in
//     one response (read-only agents run concurrently) — background also
//     satisfies it, since those calls land in one response too
//   - readOnly: a delegated edit must pass readOnly: false (verify checks the
//     edit actually landed)
// An absent argument stringifies to "", so `^(false)?$` means "not true".
